# ORDER MATTERS: _redirects is first-match-wins, so these specific rules must sit
# above the /members/:slug.html wildcard below. Otherwise the wildcard swallows
# them and rewrites to /members/<slug>, which no longer exists — a 301 into a 404.
#
# Removed from the site entirely (not just de-listed), so there is no alumni row
# to anchor to. These URLs resolve on the live site today, and §8 treats every
# currently-resolving URL as a hard requirement.
/members/gregory-quach.html  /team/  301
/members/neeraj-venna.html   /team/  301
/members/ramiz-hajj.html     /team/  301

# Jekyll served member pages at /members/<slug>.html and everything else at a
# trailing slash. Workers' default html_handling (auto-trailing-slash) already
# redirects the .html form, but with a 307 — which does not move Google's index.
# These rules pre-empt it with a real 301. _redirects is evaluated BEFORE
# html_handling, and :slug binds correctly against the .html suffix (verified).
/members/:slug.html  /members/:slug  301
/team/index.html     /team/          301
